   {
    "field": "Natural hazards",
    "order": 160,
    "content": {
     "text": "hurricanes <br /><br /><strong>volcanism:</strong> Mount Gimie (948 m), also known as Qualibou, is a caldera on the west of the island; the iconic twin pyramidal peaks of Gros Piton (771 m) and Petit Piton (743 m) are lava-dome remnants associated with the Soufrière volcano; there have been no historical magmatic eruptions, but a minor steam eruption in 1766 spread a thin layer of ash over a wide area; Saint Lucia is part of the volcanic-island arc of the Lesser Antilles that extends from Saba in the north to Grenada in the south",
     "items": []
    }
   },
   {
    "field": "Geography - note",
    "order": 170,
    "content": {
     "text": "the twin Pitons (Gros Piton and Petit Piton), striking cone-shaped peaks south of Soufrière, are one of the scenic natural highlights of the Caribbean",
     "items": []
    }
   }
